From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:14:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add deckcraft-aros: the editor in an Intuition window on
 egui-aros

Problem: the desktop app runs on eframe with wgpu, rfd, arboard and cpal,
  none of which has an AROS backend, so there is no DeckCraft window on
  AROS.
Rationale: the editor (deckcraft-ui-egui's SlideApp) is driven by the
  shared egui-aros integration (winit's contrib AROS backend, egui-winit,
  a CPU renderer, ASL requesters), as in the WordCraft, PhotoCraft and
  PdfCraft AROS ports; this crate only supplies DeckCraft's services
  (ASL open/save with the desktop app's filters, file access), the
  settings folder (PROGDIR:DeckCraftData or DECKCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR, with
  AutoRecover's folder inside it, since AROS has no HOME), a log file
  (DECKCRAFT_LOG) and a --screenshot option for unattended checks. The
  unsaved-changes prompt is the app's own (CancelClose). The process ends
  the rayon global pool before exit, because AROS's pthread library joins
  every thread in its exit handler.
Not provided, reported as unavailable rather than faked: --control (the
  localhost control server), audio output (media plays silently, the
  app's documented behaviour without an AudioOut), pictures and HTML on
  the clipboard (text goes through egui-aros), drag and drop onto the
  window, printing.
Scope: a new workspace member, not a default member; other targets build
  as before. Its egui-aros dependency resolves only through the port's
  build (scripts/dc.py patches the pinned egui-aros in); the Cargo.lock
  entries for it are written into the build copy, not here.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: x86_64 ABIv11 build links with no undefined symbols; runs
  in the port's evidence.
Removal: when DeckCraft's desktop app runs on AROS by itself.
